 the software version, in which multiple users will need access to one Master key or secret. In this case an administrator will assign a unique token/password/code for every user that he wants to allow access access to a certain part of the application with the help of tokens/passwords/code.
With the help of the two factor authentication approach an administrator has the chance of granting different levels of access for certain parts of his application, depending on a few factors:
The type of device;
The number of the factor he uses;
The number and the level of access his team has granted him so far;
The time when the activation code was last used
You can use several strategies in order to grant access based not only on a certain group but also on the time period that passed since the last time the activation code has been entered and on the number of the factors and their values, but these aspects often don’t come into consideration when it comes to creating a user’s profile/creation.
